# P2 · Doctor workspace and EMR core · Weeks 9–15 · R2 Consult
# exit: 1 ≥ 20 real visits per pilot doctor signed · 2 allergy & interaction checks fire in 100 % seeded conflicts · 3 signed notes cannot be edited (automated test) · 4 each doctor approves own Rx print layout
# nfr:  1 clinical data legal review before first real note · 2 print layouts A4/A5, 200 % zoom, screen-reader labels · 3 Rx PDF server-side, stored with hash
# pkg:  1 30-min doctor & nurse training · 2 note template pack per specialty · 3 R2 release notes + known issues
# dep:  1 formulary data source per country · 2 doctor licence verification process defined

@epic MDV-P2-E01 | Doctor Today and search | P2-01 | Doctors start the day from Today and find patients safely.
@epic MDV-P2-E02 | Patient 360, timeline and documents | P2-02, P2-07 | One verified chart with provenance on every fact and secure documents.
@epic MDV-P2-E03 | Nurse intake | P2-03 | Vitals, allergy verification and patient-reported medicines handed off to the doctor.
@epic MDV-P2-E04 | Consultation note, coding and reconciliation | P2-04, P2-05 | Write, code, reconcile and sign an immutable note; amend only by addendum.
@epic MDV-P2-E05 | Prescriptions, orders and referrals | P2-06 | Safe prescribing from a country formulary, printed multilingual Rx, investigation orders and referrals.
@epic MDV-P2-E06 | Clinical safety and R2 gate | P2-08 | Hazard log, legal review, training, templates and the R2 exit gate.

=== MDV-P2-001
title: Encounters module: start a consultation from the board/Today, bound to one patient and appointment
type: Task
epic: MDV-P2-E04
prd: P2-04
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor
labels: encounters, domain
estimate: 2
weeks: 9
depends: MDV-P1-028
confidence: 88 | Domain rules defined (one verified encounter per visit; identity banner everywhere).
sources: docs/03-architecture/modules.md; docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md
desc:
ENCOUNTER aggregate (tenant, facility, patient, lead clinician, appointment, status, started_at, authority_mode = medvya), created when the doctor calls the patient in / starts the consultation. Board state "In consult" and Today reflect it. Identity banner component bound to the encounter (name, age, sex, MRN, DOB, allergies, consent state, encounter date/room).
ac:
- Starting a consult creates exactly one active encounter for the appointment; a second start reuses it (idempotent).
- Every clinical screen in P2 shows the identity banner for the bound encounter; switching patient requires closing or explicitly leaving the encounter.
- Encounter start/end events update the reception board within 2 seconds.
- Encounter APIs require the clinician relationship/purpose policy (MDV-P2-024).

=== MDV-P2-002
title: Doctor Today (D-01): schedule, patient flags, pending notes, inbox counts
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E01
prd: P2-01
screens: D-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Solo doctor
labels: today, ui
estimate: 3
weeks: 9-10
depends: MDV-P2-001
confidence: 86 | Hi-fi Today exists for desktop and mobile; results inbox counts are placeholders until P4.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (D-01 Doctor Today); design/Medvya Mobile and Tablet (Doctor Today)
desc:
/today: today's schedule with time, name, age/sex, reason category and status chips (Seen · note signed, In room, Waiting · 12 min, Checked in · vitals done, Joined waiting room, Booked, No-show); "Next patient" hero with Start consultation; pending/unsigned notes; flags (allergy, incomplete registration); inbox counts (P4 placeholder behind flag); mine vs clinic toggle (D-04). Mobile version with bottom tabs.
ac:
- Today shows only the signed-in doctor's appointments by default and the clinic view when toggled (permissions respected).
- Unsigned notes from previous days appear as "pending notes" until signed.
- Clicking a patient opens Patient 360 for that encounter; "Start consultation" starts/opens the encounter.
- Status chips use icon + label and update live from the board.
- Mobile layout keeps the consult button in thumb reach with the next patient hero.

=== MDV-P2-003
title: Privacy-safe global search (⌘K) with care-relationship check and "Request access"
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E01
prd: P2-01
screens: D-02
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: search, privacy
estimate: 2
weeks: 10
depends: MDV-P1-018, MDV-P2-024
confidence: 88 | Designed with explicit privacy rule.
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (D-02); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#global-search-d-02
desc:
⌘K / Ctrl+K overlay: search name, MRN, phone. Results show initials + age + MRN tail until opened. Patients outside the user's care relationship show "Request access" (in clinics: request to owner; hospitals: break-glass in P7). Actions: Open chart · Start visit · Book.
ac:
- Results never include full names or identifiers before a record is opened (payload test).
- Opening a patient without a care relationship is blocked and offers Request access; the request is audited and notifies the owner.
- Keyboard: open with ⌘K/Ctrl+K, arrow navigation, Enter to open, Esc to close; screen-reader announcements.
- p95 search latency < 300 ms.

=== MDV-P2-004
title: Patient 360 (E-01): banner with identity and allergies always visible; problems, medicines, vitals trends
type: Story
epic: MDV-P2-E02
prd: P2-02
screens: E-01
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse
labels: emr, chart
estimate: 3
weeks: 10-11
depends: MDV-P2-001, MDV-P2-024
confidence: 85 | Hi-fi P360 exists; the AI-summary half ships in P3 (A-01).
sources: design/Medvya Clinician App (E-01 Patient 360); design/Medvya Mobile and Tablet (Tablet Patient 360)
desc:
/patients/:id: fixed identity banner (allergy chip never collapses; text + icon), verified chart cards: problems (with verification state), medicines (active/stopped with source), allergies, last vitals, key labs with trend mini-charts (HbA1c, BP, weight), last encounters. Start consultation in banner. Tablet two-column layout. The right-hand "AI summary · not reviewed" panel is reserved and hidden by flag until P3.
ac:
- Allergy state is shown with icon + text (e.g. "Allergy: Penicillin · verified"); "No known allergies" and "Allergies not recorded" are distinct states.
- Every chart fact shows its provenance tag (Clinician verified, Patient reported, Imported, Synced from HIS) — never an unlabelled value.
- Opening Patient 360 writes an audit event with purpose.
- Receptionist role cannot load Patient 360 (403, audited).
- Layout matches desktop and tablet designs; works at 200 % zoom.

