sources: PRD v2 P2 NFR 1; PRD v2 §10 note (P2 for clinical data)
desc:
Counsel reviews clinical data handling (purposes, consent/lawful basis, retention of notes/prescriptions per country rules, patient rights) before any real clinical note is created in production.
ac:
- Written sign-off before clinical features are enabled for real patients (flag remains off until then).
- Retention periods for notes, prescriptions and documents per country are confirmed and loaded into retention configuration.

=== MDV-P2-023
title: Define and operate the doctor licence verification process
type: Chore
epic: MDV-P2-E06
prd: P2-05
covers: dep:2
priority: MUST
roles: Medvya operations, Founder
labels: licence, operations
estimate: 0.5
weeks: 9
depends: MDV-P1-007
confidence: 75 | Process must be designed with registries per authority (NMC/state councils, DoH/DHA/MOHAP).
sources: PRD v2 P2 dependency 2; design/Medvya Access and Onboarding (F-04 licence notice)
desc:
Runbook for verifying licences: which public register per authority, evidence captured (screenshot/reference), SLA (usually within 1 working day), rejection reasons, re-verification on expiry, and who may perform it (ops vs owner attestation).
ac:
- Runbook published in docs/runbooks/licence-verification.md and linked from F-09.
- Every pilot doctor's licence is verified with recorded evidence before they sign real notes.

=== MDV-P2-024
title: Clinical authorisation: care relationship and purpose checks, request access for clinics
type: Task
epic: MDV-P2-E02
prd: P2-02
priority: MUST
roles: Doctor, Nurse, Practice owner
labels: authorisation, privacy
estimate: 2
weeks: 9-10
depends: MDV-P0-014
confidence: 84 | Matrix and principle defined; relationship rules for small clinics need a sensible default (all clinicians of the facility treat all its patients unless restricted).
sources: docs/02-design/sitemap-and-permissions.md; PRD v2 principle "Least privilege, audited"
desc:
Implement the relationship + purpose parts of the authorisation hooks from P0: a clinician has a care relationship when the patient has an appointment/encounter with them, is in their facility's active patient list (configurable clinic policy), or access was granted. Purpose is recorded with every read. Request-access workflow for clinics; hospitals' break-glass comes in P7.
ac:
- Clinicians without relationship get 403 + "Request access" (audited); owners can grant time-limited access.
- Every clinical read records purpose (treatment, registration, billing, audit).
- Clinic policy "all facility clinicians" vs "assigned only" is configurable and tested.
- Nurse access is limited per the matrix (Limited on Patient 360; entry of vitals/allergies).

